---
// THE CLOSE — ear-training. The honest, surprising reason the system earned a
// place in my week: it retrained how I hear. Not a recap of the two halves
// (the Movement pillars and §08 already did that) — the one thing left to say,
// said once, as the last words before the door.
---

<section class="ll" data-ll>
  <p class="ll-eyebrow"><span class="ll-tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>What it actually gave me</p>

  <div class="ll-lead">
    <p class="ll-big">I barely use it to finish tracks anymore. I use it to <em>hear</em>.</p>
    <p>Every master comes back with its reasons. I read which record Richard reached for, and why. I hear what it did to mine. Something rewires.</p>
    <p>Now I catch those moves everywhere. My own songs. Whatever's playing in the car. The slow, maddening part of mixing, where you run a track a dozen ways just to learn what it wants, happens in my head now. For free.</p>
    <p class="ll-kicker">It may never finish a song for me. It already taught me to hear my own.</p>
  </div>
</section>

